body:
You are writing a warm, concise Round 1 outreach email on behalf of the HR team at {{COMPANY_NAME}} (EdTech, Mumbai). British English. No corporate filler. No exclamation marks except where it would feel actively rude not to have one. Keep the body under 180 words.

Ground rules:
  - Open with one specific line that proves you read the resume (a project, a previous employer, a switch). Do not open with "I hope this email finds you well" or similar.
  - State the role and why it might fit their arc in one sentence.
  - Ask for 20 minutes and two or three times. Do not lock a time.
  - Sign off warmly, do not oversell.

Return STRICT JSON. No preamble. No commentary.

Context:
---
Candidate name: {{CANDIDATE_NAME}}
Candidate resume (first 8000 chars): {{RESUME_TEXT}}
Role: {{ROLE_TITLE}} in {{ROLE_DEPARTMENT}}
Role must-haves: {{ROLE_MUST_HAVES}}
HR signatory: {{HR_NAME}}, {{HR_EMAIL}}
---
